00:07:40.700 --> 00:07:42.950
- Yeah, so we all used to
take the bus in the morning,

00:07:42.950 --> 00:07:44.290
every morning like "we hate this."

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:45.740
Why are our parents sending us out here?

00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:47.930
We all just want to go to
our neighborhood schools.

00:07:47.930 --> 00:07:51.810
Like, so, then, fast
forward to basketball,

00:07:51.810 --> 00:07:54.605
I'm on freshman coming
off the bench out there.

00:07:54.605 --> 00:07:55.570
(Gary laughs)

00:07:55.570 --> 00:07:56.403
I'm like, I'm like.

00:07:56.403 --> 00:07:57.236
- [Gary] You hate life.

00:07:57.236 --> 00:07:58.305
- It's the worst.

00:07:58.305 --> 00:07:59.138
(Gary laughs)

00:07:59.138 --> 00:08:01.390
I think the first five to six games.

00:08:01.390 --> 00:08:03.150
- I'm sorry to interrupt you.

00:08:03.150 --> 00:08:05.930
Just knowing how successful
you've been at the NFL level,

00:08:05.930 --> 00:08:07.030
I'm so happy right now.

00:08:07.030 --> 00:08:10.720
So much of what I do is
for the 14-year-old me.

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:11.730
I had nobody to look up to.

00:08:11.730 --> 00:08:13.135
There was no entrepreneurship.

00:08:13.135 --> 00:08:13.968
- [Gary] Mhmm.

00:08:13.968 --> 00:08:15.610
- There was no cool entrepreneurship.

00:08:15.610 --> 00:08:17.110
There wasn't even entrepreneurship.

00:08:17.110 --> 00:08:18.180
I'm just so happy right now,

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:19.700
'cause I know right this second.

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:21.730
Whether it's right this
second or in four weeks

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:23.010
when somebody sees this,

00:08:23.010 --> 00:08:24.770
there's like a 15 year old

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:26.820
that just now gets to use this comp.

00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:27.950
- [Gary] Yeah.

00:08:27.950 --> 00:08:30.330
- I'm on the bench in basketball.

00:08:30.330 --> 00:08:31.163
- [Gary] Yeah.

00:08:31.163 --> 00:08:32.200
- And I think it's over,
but wait a minute, what?

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:34.508
Let me keep listening, go ahead.

00:08:34.508 --> 00:08:36.920
- So, first, I think first
game, first six games,

00:08:36.920 --> 00:08:39.490
I had come off the bench.

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:40.323
I take that back.

00:08:40.323 --> 00:08:41.840
First two games I came off the bench.

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:43.800
I came off the bench, first game I had 18.

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:46.021
Came off the bench off the second game,

00:08:46.021 --> 00:08:46.920
I had like 26.

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:47.753
- [Gary] You went crazy.

00:08:47.753 --> 00:08:49.020
- So now I'm starting.

00:08:49.020 --> 00:08:50.580
Next game I have like 25,

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:53.020
next game 26, next game like 28.

00:08:53.020 --> 00:08:55.029
Next game 30.
- [Gary] So you're balling.

00:08:55.029 --> 00:08:56.440
- Halfway through the season,

00:08:56.440 --> 00:08:57.273
I'm on JV.

00:08:57.273 --> 00:08:58.717
Mind you, I started off
freshman on the bench.

00:08:58.717 --> 00:08:59.550
- [Gary] Yeah.

00:08:59.550 --> 00:09:00.940
- So then I get moved up to JV.

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:03.620
Then I do the same
thing on JV pretty much.

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:04.620
Then like the coach comes to me,

00:09:04.620 --> 00:09:07.564
he's like look, I didn't want to start you

00:09:07.564 --> 00:09:09.210
to mess up the chemistry.

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:10.043
'Cause we already had

00:09:10.043 --> 00:09:10.876
our starting point guard and everything.

00:09:10.876 --> 00:09:12.440
But then we had like our league playoffs,

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:13.273
even though it was JV.

00:09:13.273 --> 00:09:14.704
I started for the playoffs.

00:09:14.704 --> 00:09:15.537
- [Gary] Wow.

00:09:15.537 --> 00:09:17.045
- We ended up losing the first game.

00:09:17.045 --> 00:09:19.607
But now things are kind of
starting to change a little bit.

00:09:19.607 --> 00:09:21.790
- 'Cause you're getting
some clout in school?

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:22.685
- Yeah.

00:09:22.685 --> 00:09:23.520
(Gary laughs)

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:24.642
It's more of a, yeah.

00:09:24.642 --> 00:09:25.790
- [Gary] (unintelligible) good.

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:26.760
- Yeah.

00:09:26.760 --> 00:09:27.593
- [Gary] It's flowing.

00:09:27.593 --> 00:09:29.266
- And again, it was very competitive

00:09:29.266 --> 00:09:31.400
from a sports standpoint.

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:33.110
'Cause you got a lot of kids
coming from all different

00:09:33.110 --> 00:09:35.110
places to come to this
school to play sports.

00:09:35.110 --> 00:09:37.910
So there was also two freshmen
who came in the same year

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:39.400
as me who played varsity.

00:09:39.400 --> 00:09:40.233
- Wow.

00:09:40.233 --> 00:09:42.620
- They ended up transferring
their sophomore year.

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:43.453
- [Gary] Really?

00:09:43.453 --> 00:09:45.850
- Yup, both of them ended up
transferring as sophomores.

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:47.693
- Did either one of them go on

00:09:47.693 --> 00:09:48.526
to have good college or pro careers?

00:09:48.526 --> 00:09:49.390
- No they did not.

00:09:49.390 --> 00:09:51.670
I think one of them, he
ended up playing in college.

00:09:51.670 --> 00:09:52.530
But I don't think

00:09:52.530 --> 00:09:54.240
for any big school.
- [Gary] I got you, go ahead.

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:56.960
- So then, shot out to my
boy Joan, Woody, and CJ,

00:09:56.960 --> 00:09:59.277
'cause they both were my guys.

00:09:59.277 --> 00:10:02.060
They both ended up transferring
their sophomore year.

00:10:02.060 --> 00:10:04.560
And then, that's kind of when, now.

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:05.590
- It opened up for you.

00:10:05.590 --> 00:10:07.280
- Everything started
to just kind of change,

00:10:07.280 --> 00:10:08.113
you know what I'm saying?

00:10:08.113 --> 00:10:10.430
'Cause I kind of was the
guy who was the grinder,

00:10:10.430 --> 00:10:11.263
you know what I'm saying?

00:10:11.263 --> 00:10:12.257
They came in, they played
varsity, you know what I'm saying?

00:10:12.257 --> 00:10:13.800
- They had the fucking clout,

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:14.690
they had the height.

00:10:14.690 --> 00:10:16.710
- Yeah, but everything just
kind of started to change.

00:10:16.710 --> 00:10:17.670
Then going into my sophomore year,

00:10:17.670 --> 00:10:19.410
I'm like 6'1.5" now.

00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:20.243
- [Gary] Hmm.

00:10:20.243 --> 00:10:22.021
- So I go from 5'8" to 6'1".

00:10:22.021 --> 00:10:23.523
You know.

00:10:23.523 --> 00:10:25.360
- [Gary] Five inches matter.

00:10:25.360 --> 00:10:26.668
(group laughs)

00:10:26.668 --> 00:10:28.940
- Everything starts to change.

00:10:28.940 --> 00:10:30.885
I end up playing varsity.

00:10:30.885 --> 00:10:33.611
I started off the year
on JV my sophomore year.

00:10:33.611 --> 00:10:34.444
- [Gary] Football.

00:10:34.444 --> 00:10:35.560
- I actually didn't play
football 'cause I was hurt

00:10:35.560 --> 00:10:36.603
from growth spurts.

00:10:37.460 --> 00:10:39.810
Like I couldn't do nothing,

00:10:39.810 --> 00:10:41.210
my body was just like sore.

00:10:41.210 --> 00:10:43.410
Like for real, so I didn't play football

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:44.860
my sophomore year.

00:10:44.860 --> 00:10:47.670
- Hold on, Allen Robinson,

00:10:47.670 --> 00:10:49.320
who you are right this second,

00:10:49.320 --> 00:10:51.200
did not play sophomore year?

00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:52.033
- [Allen] Nope.

00:10:52.033 --> 00:10:53.110
- On some, my body hurts.

00:10:53.110 --> 00:10:54.863
- Yeah, I couldn't run.

00:10:54.863 --> 00:10:55.696
(laughs)

00:10:55.696 --> 00:10:56.529
I couldn't run, I couldn't do nothing.

00:10:56.529 --> 00:10:58.200
- Right 'cause you change
and all of a sudden

00:10:58.200 --> 00:10:59.400
you're not a running back's body.

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:03.295
- Exactly, my whole body has changed.

00:11:03.295 --> 00:11:06.263
So I go from like 5'7",
5'8" to like 6'1.5" 6'2".

00:11:07.670 --> 00:11:09.678
So my whole body has like changed.

00:11:09.678 --> 00:11:11.420
I'm progressively getting better,

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:12.940
but like over the summer, I couldn't do

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:14.250
summer workouts and stuff.

00:11:14.250 --> 00:11:16.060
So by the time November, December hit,

00:11:16.060 --> 00:11:18.090
I'm feeling good, I'm
ready to play basketball.

00:11:18.090 --> 00:11:19.560
So then, I play basketball.

00:11:19.560 --> 00:11:20.683
I start off on JV.

00:11:21.770 --> 00:11:23.550
Those dudes kind of transfer

00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:24.383
throughout the course of the year.

00:11:24.383 --> 00:11:25.320
It's a lot of stuff.

00:11:25.320 --> 00:11:26.153
They're missing games.

00:11:26.153 --> 00:11:27.070
It's a lot going on.

00:11:27.070 --> 00:11:30.550
My school's literally like the NBA

00:11:30.550 --> 00:11:32.357
when it comes to dudes
who're like, "I don't

00:11:32.357 --> 00:11:33.190
"want to be here."

00:11:33.190 --> 00:11:34.023
You know what I'm saying?

00:11:34.023 --> 00:11:35.250
You got dudes that are like
not coming to practice.

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:36.787
- Just real shit.

00:11:36.787 --> 00:11:37.809
- They're going through
like a transfer process.

00:11:37.809 --> 00:11:39.430
They're looking at
other schools and stuff.

00:11:39.430 --> 00:11:41.250
So long story short,
they end up transferring.

00:11:41.250 --> 00:11:44.160
I get moved up to varsity
end of my sophomore year.

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:46.160
And then, in the following year,

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:47.730
now I'm on varsity, I'm 6'3".

00:11:47.730 --> 00:11:48.630
Everything's like.

00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:50.333
- [Gary] Locked.

00:11:50.333 --> 00:11:51.968
- Yeah.

00:11:51.968 --> 00:11:52.870
- Junior year football, what happens?

00:11:52.870 --> 00:11:53.819
- I have a good year.

00:11:53.819 --> 00:11:55.702
- [Gary] Wide receiver?

00:11:55.702 --> 00:11:56.774
- I play receiver.

00:11:56.774 --> 00:11:58.870
I play receiver and corner.

00:11:58.870 --> 00:12:00.360
- So you were corner and running back.

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:02.470
Prior to that, could you always catch?

00:12:02.470 --> 00:12:03.610
- I could always catch.

00:12:03.610 --> 00:12:05.900
I remember having a
conversation with my dad

00:12:05.900 --> 00:12:06.890
after hitting the growth spurt.

00:12:06.890 --> 00:12:09.260
That like, 'cause I didn't
play my sophomore year.

00:12:09.260 --> 00:12:11.950
So then that whole
spring after basketball,

00:12:11.950 --> 00:12:15.560
was like, you're about to like, receiver.

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:17.760
I'm like damn, I've played
running back my whole life.

00:12:17.760 --> 00:12:20.052
I don't know how it really is
to play receiver, you know.

00:12:20.052 --> 00:12:23.057
- Any advantages from playing
running back to receiver?

00:12:23.057 --> 00:12:25.110
- Oh, a ton.

00:12:25.110 --> 00:12:27.210
How you just see the
field and the movements

00:12:27.210 --> 00:12:28.140
and stuff is different.

00:12:28.140 --> 00:12:29.220
Even when you catch the ball

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:30.560
and how you press blocks.

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:32.210
- So one of the things that's crazy,

00:12:32.210 --> 00:12:35.100
and obviously I quadrupled
down once you signed with us.

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:38.408
Watching you, like, do you,

00:12:38.408 --> 00:12:41.310
I'm about to give you a
huge compliment, you know,

00:12:41.310 --> 00:12:43.561
in comparison to all the
Jet receivers I've watched

00:12:43.561 --> 00:12:45.080
through the years,

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:48.800
your separation sometimes
feels uncomfortable.

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:49.860
Do you think that's running back shit?

00:12:49.860 --> 00:12:51.168
- [Allen] For sure, for sure.

00:12:51.168 --> 00:12:52.684
- 'Cause you really just got it.

00:12:52.684 --> 00:12:53.788
- Being able to move,

00:12:53.788 --> 00:12:55.260
even when you catch
the ball and are seeing

00:12:55.260 --> 00:12:57.314
different angles and things like that,

00:12:57.314 --> 00:13:00.270
it's all, I would attest,
to being a running back.

00:13:00.270 --> 00:13:04.010
I played running back my whole life

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:06.360
up until my junior year in high school.

00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:09.070
So then, I played receiver my junior year,

00:13:09.070 --> 00:13:11.600
senior year, freshman year in college,

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:13.820
sophomore year, junior year in college.

00:13:13.820 --> 00:13:15.320
Before I got to the NFL,
that was the only time

00:13:15.320 --> 00:13:18.030
I played receiver, was
like, those five years.

00:13:18.030 --> 00:13:19.573
- When did it click, receiver?

00:13:20.494 --> 00:13:21.327
(Allen sighs)

00:13:21.327 --> 00:13:23.980
- I would probably say
going into my senior year.

00:13:23.980 --> 00:13:25.530
- During that spring and summer?

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:27.200
- Yeah, during that spring it clicked.

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:29.630
I would say basketball too, both.

00:13:29.630 --> 00:13:33.047
- Did you think as a freshman or sophomore

00:13:33.047 --> 00:13:34.780
you were going to be a basketball player?

00:13:34.780 --> 00:13:37.720
- For sure, me and one
of my high school coaches

00:13:37.720 --> 00:13:40.100
used to have a bet, used
to tell me your first offer

00:13:40.100 --> 00:13:42.530
is gonna come from, from
like your first big offer's

00:13:42.530 --> 00:13:43.803
gonna come from football
before basketball.

00:13:43.803 --> 00:13:45.690
We were always going
back and forth with it.

00:13:45.690 --> 00:13:49.710
And like, going into my
senior year, my junior year,

00:13:49.710 --> 00:13:51.650
I'm literally taking a nap.

00:13:51.650 --> 00:13:52.850
He like, texts me a number.

00:13:52.850 --> 00:13:53.980
He's like, "yo, call this number."

00:13:53.980 --> 00:13:55.940
So I call the number,
they answer the phone.

00:13:55.940 --> 00:13:58.720
It's the Minnesota coaching staff.

00:13:58.720 --> 00:14:00.400
And that was my first offer.

00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:02.540
Actually my first offer
was a Big Ten offer.

00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:03.720
- [Gary] That's cool.

00:14:03.720 --> 00:14:05.610
- So after that, everything just changed.

00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:07.021
It got real, because my parents,

00:14:07.021 --> 00:14:08.621
and shout out to my parents 'cause

00:14:08.621 --> 00:14:10.143
throughout the whole process,

00:14:10.143 --> 00:14:12.690
like my mom, still at my house right now,

00:14:12.690 --> 00:14:16.210
has like a whole thick book of everybody

00:14:16.210 --> 00:14:17.853
that like sent me letters,
the places, the schools

00:14:17.853 --> 00:14:21.500
that I wanted to go to,
sending out questionnaires.

00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:23.842
Us sending out highlight
tapes, things like that.

00:14:23.842 --> 00:14:26.079
Sending them to different
schools and stuff.

00:14:26.079 --> 00:14:30.210
My parents definitely
were heavily involved.

00:14:30.210 --> 00:14:32.200
- Were your parents athletes?

00:14:32.200 --> 00:14:33.823
- They were not, they were not.

00:14:33.823 --> 00:14:35.600
I just think that, for
my parents, you know,

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:38.353
from five years old, I had been,

00:14:38.353 --> 00:14:41.150
probably even before that, one of the most

00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:45.600
competitive kids in sports,
that like, you probably could,

00:14:45.600 --> 00:14:47.050
- Did you cry when you lost?

00:14:47.050 --> 00:14:48.760
- Of course.

00:14:48.760 --> 00:14:51.770
- I cried basically until I was like 12

00:14:51.770 --> 00:14:53.230
if I lost at anything.

00:14:53.230 --> 00:14:55.940
I was also so confident I was delusional.

00:14:55.940 --> 00:14:56.773
- [Allen] Same.

00:14:56.773 --> 00:14:58.830
- I cried 'cause I was
stunned I didn't win.

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:00.110
- Same, same.

00:15:00.110 --> 00:15:02.380
I remember, it used to be so bad.

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:03.511
And my dad was like look.

00:15:03.511 --> 00:15:05.690
You win a lot of games.

00:15:05.690 --> 00:15:06.523
- [Gary] Stop crying.

00:15:06.523 --> 00:15:08.103
- Yeah like you win a lot of games.

00:15:08.103 --> 00:15:09.179
(laughs)

00:15:09.179 --> 00:15:12.057
I always tell people,
you know, having kids,

00:15:12.057 --> 00:15:15.070
and like having, I don't
know how I would want

00:15:15.070 --> 00:15:18.030
to introduce sports to my kids.

00:15:18.030 --> 00:15:19.930
- Well there's a huge different variable.

00:15:19.930 --> 00:15:21.730
When I was doing a wine
show on the internet

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:23.130
back in the day, I had Wayne Gretzky

00:15:23.130 --> 00:15:24.530
on 'cause he had a wine,

00:15:24.530 --> 00:15:27.200
which is super cool, greatest
hockey player of all time.

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:29.780
And, super funny story, there is people

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:32.414
before we got on set, were
like Wayne's very introverted.

00:15:32.414 --> 00:15:34.311
He's not going to say what's up.

00:15:34.311 --> 00:15:36.130
It's not bad, just don't worry about him.

00:15:36.130 --> 00:15:36.963
I'm like cool.

00:15:36.963 --> 00:15:38.830
Of course I'm thinking I'm
the most charismatic fucker

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:40.760
on earth, we're gonna be
best friends in two minutes.

00:15:40.760 --> 00:15:43.880
Sure enough, just one little opening,

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:44.713
and I didn't know this.

00:15:44.713 --> 00:15:46.220
I didn't know this, 'cause
I don't do homework.

00:15:46.220 --> 00:15:47.293
I mention that I was from Belarus,

00:15:47.293 --> 00:15:49.760
he's like, "my
grandfather's from Belarus."

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:51.150
Which is cool, 'cause I didn't know,

00:15:51.150 --> 00:15:52.490
and like the greatest hockey player

00:15:52.490 --> 00:15:54.600
having Russian descent makes sense.

00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:55.640
We got into a conversation then

00:15:55.640 --> 00:15:58.715
'cause there was something
wrong with a camera actually.

00:15:58.715 --> 00:16:00.900
Somehow we got into him saying

00:16:00.900 --> 00:16:04.163
that he wouldn't let his kids play hockey.

00:16:05.190 --> 00:16:06.840
And I thought it was super fresh.

00:16:08.425 --> 00:16:11.032
And that's, with your story.

00:16:11.032 --> 00:16:12.710
Same with me as an entrepreneur,

00:16:12.710 --> 00:16:15.310
I think every day about
my daughter and son.

00:16:15.310 --> 00:16:17.230
I'm like, I'm not gonna pressure them

00:16:17.230 --> 00:16:18.820
to be an entrepreneur
and I'm not even sure

00:16:18.820 --> 00:16:21.685
I want them to be, because
you know what happens.

00:16:21.685 --> 00:16:22.768
- [Allen] Yeah.

00:16:22.768 --> 00:16:23.826
- It's gonna be comparison city.

00:16:23.826 --> 00:16:25.460
Now, in baseball, we have
a whole wave right now

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:28.550
of kids who are coming
