00:28:49.261 --> 00:28:50.800
- [Caller] Yeah, Chattanooga.

00:28:50.800 --> 00:28:51.970
- Yup, thank you bro.

00:28:51.970 --> 00:28:53.960
What's your question?

00:28:53.960 --> 00:28:55.350
- [Caller] I just heard
Allen talking about

00:28:55.350 --> 00:28:58.830
how he was also really
passionate about basketball

00:28:58.830 --> 00:29:01.410
at one time, in high school playing both,

00:29:01.410 --> 00:29:04.080
and seeing like a future in basketball.

00:29:04.080 --> 00:29:06.070
And I was just curious,
I know a lot of athletes

00:29:06.070 --> 00:29:07.240
are better at one sport.

00:29:07.240 --> 00:29:09.340
People push them towards one sport more,

00:29:09.340 --> 00:29:12.103
but they may like the other sport better.

00:29:13.100 --> 00:29:14.480
I had a friend like that in high school

00:29:14.480 --> 00:29:15.800
who went to go play in Miami,

00:29:15.800 --> 00:29:17.590
just because he could play
football and basketball

00:29:17.590 --> 00:29:18.890
at the same time.

00:29:18.890 --> 00:29:20.740
That was like very important to him.

00:29:20.740 --> 00:29:21.573
- Understood.

00:29:21.573 --> 00:29:23.554
- [Caller] So I was just curious about,

00:29:23.554 --> 00:29:27.150
kind of the same thing
for entrepreneurship,

00:29:27.150 --> 00:29:30.960
you lean into what
everybody's pushing towards,

00:29:30.960 --> 00:29:32.100
or what they could be better at.

00:29:32.100 --> 00:29:32.973
- Or where you think the money is.

00:29:32.973 --> 00:29:35.240
- [Caller] Or what you're
more passionate about.

00:29:35.240 --> 00:29:36.853
- That's a great question.

00:29:36.853 --> 00:29:40.340
Allen, did you, how did you
personally think about that?

00:29:40.340 --> 00:29:41.620
You loved basketball.

00:29:41.620 --> 00:29:43.100
- To this day, I love basketball.

00:29:43.100 --> 00:29:43.970
- I know, I watched you last night.

00:29:43.970 --> 00:29:45.550
- To be honest, I'll watch.

00:29:45.550 --> 00:29:47.895
- A basketball game over a football game

00:29:47.895 --> 00:29:48.934
any day of the week.

00:29:48.934 --> 00:29:49.860
- For sure, for sure.

00:29:49.860 --> 00:29:51.580
When it gets around playoff
time it's kinda different,

00:29:51.580 --> 00:29:52.440
you know what I'm saying.

00:29:52.440 --> 00:29:55.164
I'm like actually immersed in the NFL.

00:29:55.164 --> 00:29:55.997
- [Gary] Of course.

00:29:55.997 --> 00:29:57.990
- After playing in the
playoffs and things like that.

00:29:57.990 --> 00:30:00.610
Yeah, so, but for me, basketball

00:30:00.610 --> 00:30:01.740
I would probably say was pushed more.

00:30:01.740 --> 00:30:03.171
- How much did you,

00:30:03.171 --> 00:30:04.300
- [Allen] 100 times.

00:30:04.300 --> 00:30:08.200
- Debate not, when you
went, so what happened?

00:30:08.200 --> 00:30:10.700
What was your most
serious basketball offer?

00:30:10.700 --> 00:30:12.340
- My high school coach
told me I could've gone

00:30:12.340 --> 00:30:13.173
to Michigan State and played both.

00:30:13.173 --> 00:30:15.070
There actually was a guy named Dion Sims,

00:30:15.070 --> 00:30:17.050
shout out to Dion, who I
played in Chicago with as well,

00:30:17.050 --> 00:30:17.883
he went to my high school,

00:30:17.883 --> 00:30:18.716
he went to Michigan State.

00:30:18.716 --> 00:30:19.830
He played both.

00:30:19.830 --> 00:30:20.663
You know, so.

00:30:20.663 --> 00:30:22.480
- So what made you go to Penn State?

00:30:22.480 --> 00:30:24.429
- I wanted to play football.

00:30:24.429 --> 00:30:25.262
- At that point in your life.

00:30:25.262 --> 00:30:27.250
- Going to my senior year, I had decided.

00:30:28.540 --> 00:30:30.590
I said I was gonna play
football in college.

00:30:30.590 --> 00:30:31.440
- [Gary] Because?

00:30:33.060 --> 00:30:34.040
- Honestly, honestly.

00:30:34.040 --> 00:30:35.835
- This is actually a great
question that he's asking.

00:30:35.835 --> 00:30:36.668
I have a feeling you're
about to answer this,

00:30:36.668 --> 00:30:37.783
this is a good moment: why?

00:30:38.820 --> 00:30:41.370
- Football was just, it was easier.

00:30:41.370 --> 00:30:43.836
Not easier in the sense
like, it was easier to do.

00:30:43.836 --> 00:30:44.669
- [Gary] You were better at it.

00:30:44.669 --> 00:30:45.560
But for me on the field.

00:30:45.560 --> 00:30:46.393
- [Gary] You were better at it.

00:30:46.393 --> 00:30:47.456
- Way better at it.

00:30:47.456 --> 00:30:49.450
The game became easier for me.

00:30:49.450 --> 00:30:50.690
- So let's talk about it.

00:30:50.690 --> 00:30:55.690
Does that mean you chose a
path that gave you confidence,

00:30:56.160 --> 00:30:57.539
could lead to financial and

00:30:57.539 --> 00:30:59.400
professional success?
- [Allen] For sure, for sure.

00:30:59.400 --> 00:31:03.500
- Over what probably, it's pretty obvious,

00:31:03.500 --> 00:31:05.960
especially in the last 48
hours I've been with you,

00:31:05.960 --> 00:31:07.750
basketball was a bigger love.

00:31:07.750 --> 00:31:10.733
- For sure, but I think that
once I started my senior year,

00:31:10.733 --> 00:31:12.150
when I started to dive in.

00:31:12.150 --> 00:31:14.530
'Cause I had a really good
senior year in basketball,

00:31:14.530 --> 00:31:16.310
but once I started to dive in to football,

00:31:16.310 --> 00:31:18.620
and really put my mind there,

00:31:18.620 --> 00:31:19.970
going into my senior year.

00:31:19.970 --> 00:31:22.680
For me, I was all in it, you know?

00:31:22.680 --> 00:31:23.513
- [Allen] Got it.

00:31:23.513 --> 00:31:25.950
- I still have a weird love for it.

00:31:25.950 --> 00:31:27.565
But I don't know.

00:31:27.565 --> 00:31:29.070
It was just different when
it came to like football,

00:31:29.070 --> 00:31:29.903
you know what I'm saying?

00:31:29.903 --> 00:31:30.736
When I would step on the field,

00:31:30.736 --> 00:31:32.830
just my craft, and how I would perfect it.

00:31:32.830 --> 00:31:33.663
- [Gary] You just knew.

00:31:33.663 --> 00:31:35.960
- It was a lot different,
it was a lot different.

00:31:35.960 --> 00:31:36.793
- Interesting.

00:31:36.793 --> 00:31:39.520
- It's so different that
it's hard to explain.

00:31:39.520 --> 00:31:40.353
I tell people all the time.

00:31:40.353 --> 00:31:41.753
I never, I don't remember the last time

00:31:41.753 --> 00:31:43.570
I actually picked up
a basketball or played

00:31:43.570 --> 00:31:44.403
five on five or something,

00:31:44.403 --> 00:31:46.820
just 'cause my passion
and my love for the game

00:31:46.820 --> 00:31:48.920
is so high, so intense,
you know what I'm saying?

00:31:48.920 --> 00:31:50.398
I wouldn't even want to put myself,

00:31:50.398 --> 00:31:52.530
let's go to the rec and play five on five.

00:31:52.530 --> 00:31:54.420
'Cause I may not leave.

00:31:54.420 --> 00:31:55.300
- I get that.

00:31:55.300 --> 00:31:57.040
It's almost how I think about meditation.

00:31:57.040 --> 00:31:57.873
- [Allen] Yeah.

00:31:57.873 --> 00:31:58.706
- I don't want to meditate,

00:31:58.706 --> 00:32:01.210
'cause I'm so happy with my mental state.

00:32:01.210 --> 00:32:03.526
I almost weirdly understand
what you just said.

00:32:03.526 --> 00:32:04.620
- So it's like.

00:32:04.620 --> 00:32:06.360
- The normal person kind of hears that,

00:32:06.360 --> 00:32:08.480
like you don't even want to play a random

00:32:08.480 --> 00:32:11.480
basketball game 'cause you
know you might get in it.

00:32:11.480 --> 00:32:13.077
- Exactly, you know how
people talk about Jordan,

00:32:13.077 --> 00:32:14.581
and they joke about Jordan,

00:32:14.581 --> 00:32:17.250
they say like Michael
Jordan had these card games,

00:32:17.250 --> 00:32:18.660
he wouldn't let the person leave.

00:32:18.660 --> 00:32:20.237
They'll be there for like-

00:32:20.237 --> 00:32:21.070
- Yeah, 21.

00:32:21.070 --> 00:32:22.043
- That's how I feel about
basketball, so it's like-

00:32:22.043 --> 00:32:24.120
- I have a great Jets-Bears story.

00:32:24.120 --> 00:32:25.820
I told it the other day,
I think you guys heard it.

00:32:25.820 --> 00:32:28.247
My best friend Brandon
was a Cubs fan, baseball.

00:32:28.247 --> 00:32:30.091
And we had baseball cards together.

00:32:30.091 --> 00:32:30.924
- [Allen] Mhmm.

00:32:30.924 --> 00:32:31.970
- And he came over one night to sleep over

00:32:31.970 --> 00:32:33.810
the night before a baseball card show,

00:32:33.810 --> 00:32:35.090
and we played Madden.

00:32:35.090 --> 00:32:36.460
And he took the Bears,
he didn't give a fuck

00:32:36.460 --> 00:32:37.490
about the Bears.

00:32:37.490 --> 00:32:39.290
He was Chicago, 'cause he was Cubs.

00:32:39.290 --> 00:32:41.270
And some miraculous way he beat me

00:32:41.270 --> 00:32:43.267
after I like destroyed
him every other time.

00:32:43.267 --> 00:32:44.600
And I wouldn't let him go to sleep.

00:32:44.600 --> 00:32:45.433
It was like midnight.

00:32:45.433 --> 00:32:47.290
And I wouldn't let him go to
sleep until we re-matched.

00:32:47.290 --> 00:32:49.670
And then I could tell he was bullshitting,

00:32:49.670 --> 00:32:51.690
'cause he was mad that I
was forcing him to play.

00:32:51.690 --> 00:32:53.280
So he was like not trying.

00:32:53.280 --> 00:32:55.810
But then I countered it
with like making pretend

00:32:55.810 --> 00:32:58.340
he was trying and blew him
out like 72 to nothing.

00:32:58.340 --> 00:33:01.070
And was like in his face at like 2:00 a.m.

00:33:01.070 --> 00:33:01.903
- [Allen] Exactly.

00:33:01.903 --> 00:33:03.480
- Exactly.

00:33:03.480 --> 00:33:05.880
- And it's crazy because
the last kind of serious

00:33:05.880 --> 00:33:08.470
that I played, was an intramural.

00:33:08.470 --> 00:33:11.480
Not intramural, but basketball
class at Penn State.

00:33:11.480 --> 00:33:12.470
We had a basketball class.

00:33:12.470 --> 00:33:13.303
